            <title>[LU-21007] lctl get_param -n -y prints the name of a multi-line parameter</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21007</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lctl get_param -n -y&lt;/tt&gt; prints the parameter name for a multi-line value. The &lt;tt&gt;-n&lt;/tt&gt; option must print only the value. For a single-line value, &lt;tt&gt;-n -y&lt;/tt&gt; prints only the value, as expected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master, 2.17.0 and later.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The defect started with commit 5768bf35fd ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18502" title="YAML import and export for nodemaps" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18502"&gt;LU-18502&lt;/a&gt; utils: Support YAML for get_param parameter names", &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/58113" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/58113&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;On the MGS, create a nodemap with 2 idmaps: &lt;tt&gt;lctl nodemap_add c0&lt;/tt&gt;, then &lt;tt&gt;lctl nodemap_add_idmap --name c0 --idtype uid --idmap 1003:11000&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;lctl nodemap_add_idmap --name c0 --idtype gid --idmap 1003:11000&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;tt&gt;lctl get_param -n -y nodemap.c0.idmap&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Expected output is the value only:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[
 { idtype: uid, client_id: 1003, fs_id: 11000 },
 { idtype: gid, client_id: 1003, fs_id: 11000 }
]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Actual output starts with the name:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;nodemap.c0.idmap: [
 { idtype: uid, client_id: 1003, fs_id: 11000 },
 { idtype: gid, client_id: 1003, fs_id: 11000 }
]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This result comes from a source review. We did not run the reproduction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Analysis"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Analysis&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;tt&gt;print_param_internal()&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;lustre/utils/lustre_param.c&lt;/tt&gt;, the multi-line branch runs when &lt;tt&gt;po_yaml&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;po_header&lt;/tt&gt; is set. That branch prints &lt;tt&gt;lpf_name&lt;/tt&gt; on the first line and does not check &lt;tt&gt;po_show_name&lt;/tt&gt;. The single-line branch (the &lt;tt&gt;else&lt;/tt&gt; branch) prints the name only when &lt;tt&gt;po_show_name&lt;/tt&gt; is set.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before 5768bf35fd, only &lt;tt&gt;po_header&lt;/tt&gt; selected the multi-line branch. A &lt;tt&gt;-n -y&lt;/tt&gt; request went to the single-line branch, so it printed only the value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The AI review of &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69687" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69687&lt;/a&gt; found this defect. 69687 indents the lines of a multi-line value for &lt;tt&gt;-y&lt;/tt&gt;, so with &lt;tt&gt;-n&lt;/tt&gt; the output now also has the indent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Proposedfix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the multi-line branch, print the name and the separator only when &lt;tt&gt;po_show_name&lt;/tt&gt; is set. When &lt;tt&gt;po_show_name&lt;/tt&gt; is clear, print the value without the name and without the extra indent. Add a &lt;tt&gt;-n -y&lt;/tt&gt; case for a multi-line parameter to sanity-sec test_25c.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
